 this task as requiring an LLM or claim broad inference advances."],"id":"study-learned-gated-slice-v1","invariants":["Same admitted model, tokenizer/template, output ceiling, sampling, offered task population and paired order.","Candidate consumes prompt text only. Expected answers are independently evaluated after inference.","Every failed, interrupted and missing request remains charged and in the offered denominator."],"kind":"new_combination","mechanism":"Fit a depth-two empirical harmful-omission tree on actual paired native outcomes, select a threshold on separate table-group calibration data, then route frozen confirmation prompts using graph features only. No feasible calibration point falls back to full context.","mechanism_id":"learned-gated-slice-v1","metrics":[{"decision_rule":"At least 5% improvement in every balanced pair, with quality gates and at most 10% p95/p99 tail regression; descriptive ranges, not significance.","direction":"lower","name":"full_attempt_wall","unit":"nanoseconds"},{"decision_rule":"Include setup, development/search, failed attempts, preprocessing and retries; shared ancestry is counted once.","direction":"lower","name":"all_allocation_cost","unit":"nanoseconds"},{"decision_rule":"95% absolute minimum and zero allowed observed pairwise quality regression.","direction":"higher","name":"task_accuracy","unit":"fraction_of_offered_requests"}],"novelty":{"search_scope":"Primary RECOMP, LLMLingua-2, Context Codec and SLICET5 pages reviewed 2026-09-08; classical dependency slicing is existing work. This bounded test does not establish priority. Related selective prediction and routing: Learn then Test https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.01052; Conformal Risk Control https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.02814; RouteLLM https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.18665. This empirical procedure has no conformal or population-risk guarantee.","status":"OVERLAP_IDENTIFIED","unresolved_questions":["Whether a syntax/dependency certificate predicts model task accuracy or cost advantage on the declared structured-record population."]},"objective":"efficiency_at_quality","prediction":"Model-bound empirical acceptance may avoid harmful omissions while retaining useful slicing savings, but calibration failure, distribution shift and full training/setup cost may erase the benefit.","prior_art":[{"overlap":"Extractive and abstractive compression before language-model inference; existing compression/selection baseline, not a local reproduction.","proposed_difference":"A small registered record-language closure/certificate/fallback implementation and its real-model causal ablations; no priority claim and no replication of the paper benchmark.","source_id":"src-e328bbedf98a"},{"overlap":"Learned extractive prompt compression via token classification; overlaps the general aim of preserving useful information while shortening prompts.","proposed_difference":"A small registered record-language closure/certificate/fallback implementation and its real-model causal ablations; no priority claim and no replication of the paper benchmark.","source_id":"src-31ff4c063d85"},{"overlap":"Commitment-level representation, verification and conservative fallbacks; closest recent conceptual overlap, not a guarantee of unchanged model outputs.","proposed_difference":"A small registered record-language closure/certificate/fallback implementation and its real-model causal ablations; no priority claim and no replication of the paper benchmark.","source_id":"src-3c432f15c030"},{"overlap":"Learned static slicing with dependency identification and constrained generation; overlaps source-grounded dependency selection, with different model and task scope.","proposed_difference":"A small registered record-language closure/certificate/fallback implementation and its real-model causal ablations; no priority claim and no replication of the paper benchmark.","source_id":"src-b7b2127b7c85"}],"quality_contract":{"decision_rule":"Both arms at least 95% correct on every offered reque